    },
    "body": "The prior 128-row cue fit improved development but none of its changed addresses reached the diagnostic holdout. This change adds a fixed prospective composition panel: 512 development/128 evaluation rows from disjoint banks of retained familiar literals, crossed roles and record order, with two actual Source candidates admitted throughout. It preserves duplicate/public-tokenization guards and fixes two real donor/order preparation defects rather than relaxing the instrument.\n\nThe new native discrete fit accepts eight quarter updates. Development source selection improves258→271/512 and complete own-prefix answers40→51/512. Prospective source67/128, first token62/128 and complete answers15/128 remain unchanged in aggregate (one complete gain/one loss). Changed coefficients reach36 evaluation reads; correct-source margins improve24 and worsen10 without crossings. This is one trajectory and structured familiar-language composition, not general chat or replicated transfer qualification. Runtime receives the two current records, not full chronology.\n\nThe fit's final report write exposed a hardcoded512MiB ceiling masking its admitted1GiB limit. Generic writes now use the admitted default while explicit narrower limits remain enforced. A new manifest/config-bound evaluation-only completion restores the missing selected generation in a separate sealed root with zero additional gradients, proposals or updates. The failed sealed attempt remains preserved.\n\nValidation at numerical head f254565a7db470886003451cf4a201deb678260c: independent source review; rustfmt; release39 bank-fit,16 plan,25 panel and46 sibling observation tests; all three release drivers built. Canonical Linux x86 pod, CPU8,98.323s. Actual wrong-manifest rejection and valid completion PASS (17.281s, CPU16,5.05GB peak owned RSS); frozen source/prefix/end and immutable input checks pass. Source bytes bound by2451-entry inventory; no laptop builds or GPU/Metal model claims. Final3a5eb343 changes only docs; claim-wording check passes.\n\nDurable canonical evidence: /workspace/uor-r4/codex/cue-composition/{panel-development-3,panel-fresh-3,checks-4,checks-5,discrete-fit-1,discrete-completion-1,analysis-1}. Completion manifest6b4882752f2274d4d8f2554ce8098ebe81ca0f36a811f0ea959c3187691b9c67; selected cue7c577ec5ce6d0d20b10a999752febc40a0e490af9e56474df4ab472be452265f. Next is fixed-selected-checkpoint signed-credit/conflict attribution, not an unchanged longer fit.\n\nStacked on PR1760. References #820 and #1552; does not close geometric attention. No shared session/compiler files changed.\n",
